# Security headers for the editor, the preview, published apps' page and every built asset. The Worker sets the same
# ones itself (packages/worker/src/http.ts, PAGE_HEADERS; a test checks they match), since it answers every request
# first and Cloudflare applies this file only to assets it serves itself. `vite preview` applies it too (the e2e tests
# fail on any policy violation); `vite dev` doesn't, so hot reloading still works. /api answers get their own
# (packages/worker/src/http.ts, API_HEADERS).
#
# style-src has no 'unsafe-inline': Vue sets style bindings through the DOM, which the policy allows, but it would turn
# large static templates (the illustrations' `style="fill: var(…)"`) into HTML strings, whose style attributes it
# refuses. vueCompilerOptions.ts turns that off (hoistStatic; test/csp.test.ts checks it holds). img-src takes any https image, since model images can be anywhere;
# connect-src any https address, since data resources fetch from the browser.
/*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'self'; script-src 'self'; style-src 'self'; font-src 'self'; img-src 'self' data: https:; connect-src 'self' https:; object-src 'none'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'none'; frame-ancestors 'none'
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: no-referrer
  Permissions-Policy: camera=(), microphone=(), geolocation=()
  Cross-Origin-Opener-Policy: same-origin
